From cce7ef7cfaafd861c16d1db886c664dd70cc6b7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Trung=20L=C3=AA?= <8@tle.id.au>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:51:51 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 13/25] Add an AltiVec path for the 2D swizzle routines on
 PowerPC

The premultiply, unpremultiply, swizzle and RGB24 unpack row and surface
operations in gfx/2d had SSE2, SSSE3, AVX2 and NEON kernels and ran the
scalar fallbacks on PowerPC. SwizzleAltiVec.cpp adds kernels built from
the VMX subset so they serve the PowerPC 970 as well as POWER8 and later,
selected at run time through supports_vmx().

The arithmetic reproduces the scalar fallbacks exactly: premultiply uses
c * a + 255 followed by the (c + (c >> 8)) >> 8 divide, and unpremultiply
uses the 8.16 reciprocal table with a truncating (c * q) >> 16, formed from
two 16x16 multiply-sums since AltiVec has no 32-bit multiply. The even
(B/R) and odd (G/A) channels are split into 16-bit lanes with an endian
switch, so the kernels are correct on big-endian targets too. Loads and
stores use the VSX unaligned forms when available and the lvsl/vperm and
rotate plus vec_ste idioms on plain AltiVec.
